// The shape of the site: generated data, not hand-written code. Everything is in metres, on the
// ground plane x (east) and z (south), with y up. The tools that made it are not part of this
// repository, so treat it as an asset: change it only together with the 3D models that draw the same
// ground (assets/models/terrain.glb and site.glb), or trucks will hover over or sink into the road.
// This file is left out of prettier on purpose (see .prettierignore): one value per line would be
// thousands of lines.
//
//   FIELD_N, FIELD_CELL, FIELD_ORIGIN  the height field is FIELD_N x FIELD_N samples, FIELD_CELL metres
//                                      apart, starting at FIELD_ORIGIN on both axes (-240 m to +240 m).
//   HEIGHTS      ground height at each sample, row by row: HEIGHTS[row * FIELD_N + column], where the
//                row steps along z and the column along x. heightAt() in world/terrain.logic
//                interpolates between samples.
//   HAUL_PATH    the haul road's centre line as [x, y, z] points, from the loading bay at Bench 1 up
//                the ramp to the crusher. Trucks drive it (mine/route.logic) and the map draws it.
//   SOLIDS       buildings and walls as boxes: [centre x, centre z, width along x, depth along z].
//   ROCK_BOUNDS  rock outcrops: [centre x, centre z, width, depth, base height, height].
//   BERMS        safety berms along the road edge: [x1, z1, x2, z2, half-width].
